/**
 * The fetch/verify/install contract (docs/fetch.md), tested offline.
 *
 * Two kinds of release drive it:
 *
 *  - synthetic ones, built here with a test-only ed25519 key and a hand
 *    ustar writer, so every link of the chain can be broken on purpose
 *    (bad signature, unsigned, tampered tarball, index/sums disagreement,
 *    manifest/index disagreement, path traversal) and the verdict checked;
 *  - the shared vectors under `spec/fixtures/fetch/` (§9), generated by the
 *    core repository's tooling, which every SDK must pass with the same
 *    codes. When they are absent this block SKIPS LOUDLY — never silently.
 *
 * Nothing here asserts on an exit code alone: every verdict is checked by
 * its error class and code, and every install by what is on disk.
 *
 * The fake libraries are random bytes: they hash correctly and can never
 * dlopen, which is exactly the property the autofetch tests need — a fetch
 * that ran is proven by the loader's own "cannot load" on the bytes it
 * installed, at the directory the search path says.
 */

